#
# Moonwater compositor present, ordinary terminal first
#
# Canvas remains compiled and its window/Spark ABI remains available, but it
# does not probe or claim a DRM device during boot. PID 1's supervised shell
# therefore stays directly on /dev/console. This is useful when programs need
# the Canvas/window ABI but the machine must boot console-first, and for
# separating compositor startup from the rest of the base-system boot.
#
# Compose this after gpu so these last requests win:
#
#   sh build.sh arch/x64 debug_none limbo desktop serial terminal
#
CONFIG_MOONWATER_CANVAS=y
CONFIG_MOONWATER_CANVAS_AUTOSTART=n

# gpu's built-in command line suppresses the DRM fbdev client specifically so
# Canvas can own the display. With Canvas dormant, let fbcon attach normally.
CONFIG_DRM_FBDEV_EMULATION=y
CONFIG_FB=y
CONFIG_FRAMEBUFFER_CONSOLE=y
CONFIG_VT=y
CONFIG_VT_CONSOLE=y

# The built-in command line otherwise tells the fbdev client to stay away,
# which would leave this image with nothing on screen either; the rest of it
# (the pstate, hash and swiotlb words) stays.
#> cmdline -drm_client_lib.active=
